# Example ReRDMFT input file: LiH, 6-31G, MULLER (a JK-only functional), 4-component min-max stage with
# Cholesky vectors (CHOLESKY TRUE). Same two stages as lih_gnof_c4_neg_full_optimization.inp: the
# positive-energy-only minimization (here with ADAM), then the min-max stage (NEO, saddle point of the order set
# by the occupied positive-energy spinors -- 484 Kramers-reduced electron-positron parameters here). The stage
# needs the negative-energy block of the MO Cholesky vectors, which the first stage drops; they are built
# separately only when FULL_OPTIMIZATION_4C_NEG is TRUE. DEBUG TRUE (set here) adds the dense-diagonalization
# count of the negative Hessian eigenvalues (484 expected, "[PASS] the point is a saddle of order 484") and the other
# DEBUG checks. Measured: ~26 s with DEBUG (~7 s without it: remove the DEBUG line for a quick run).
NELEC 4
BASIS lih-6-31g.gbs
C4_SPINOR TRUE
FUNCTIONAL MULLER
CHOLESKY TRUE
FULL_OPTIMIZATION TRUE
FULL_OPTIMIZATION_4C_NEG TRUE
DEBUG TRUE

GEOMETRY
Li  0.000000   0.000000   0.000000
H   0.000000   0.000000   1.594900
END
